<article class="prose">
  <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
  <p class="text-muted">Policy version <%= cookiePolicyVersion %>. This policy explains what cookies are, which ones <%= siteName %> uses, and how you can control them.</p>

  <h2>What are cookies?</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files that a website stores in your browser. Some are essential for the site
    to work (for example, to keep you logged in). Others are optional and are used for things like
    statistics or advertising. Under the EU ePrivacy Directive and the GDPR we may only set optional
    cookies after you have actively agreed to them.
  </p>

  <h2>How we ask for consent</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>On your first visit we show a banner with three equal choices: <strong>Accept all</strong>, <strong>Reject non-essential</strong> and <strong>Customize</strong>.</li>
    <li>Optional categories are <strong>switched off by default</strong> - nothing is pre-ticked.</li>
    <li>Scrolling, clicking elsewhere or ignoring the banner is <strong>not</strong> treated as consent.</li>
    <li>No analytics or advertising scripts are loaded until you allow the matching category.</li>
    <li>If you reject optional cookies, the whole site still works normally.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies we use</h2>
  <% cookieCatalog.forEach((cat) => { %>
    <section class="policy-category">
      <h3>
        <%= cat.title %>
        <span class="badge <%= cat.required ? 'badge-neutral' : 'badge-optional' %>"><%= cat.required ? 'Essential - no consent needed' : 'Optional - requires consent' %></span>
      </h3>
      <p><%= cat.description %></p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="table">
          <caption class="visually-hidden"><%= cat.title %> cookies</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Duration</th><th scope="col">Provider</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <% cat.cookies.forEach((c) => { %>
              <tr>
                <td data-label="Name"><code><%= c.name %></code></td>
                <td data-label="Purpose"><%= c.purpose %></td>
                <td data-label="Duration"><%= c.duration %></td>
                <td data-label="Provider"><%= c.provider %></td>
              </tr>
            <% }) %>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
  <% }) %>

  <p class="text-muted small">
    In this demo the analytics and marketing "providers" are simulated local scripts
    (<code>/js/vendor/</code>) that only set a cookie and write to the browser console. They stand in for
    real third-party tools to show that nothing loads before consent.
  </p>

  <h2 id="manage">How to change or withdraw your consent</h2>
  <p>
    You can change your choices at any time, and withdrawing consent is as easy as giving it.
    Use the <strong>Cookie Settings</strong> link in the footer of every page, or the button below.
    When you withdraw consent we delete the related optional cookies straight away; scripts that were
    already running stop completely the next time a page loads.
  </p>
  <p>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-open-cookie-settings>Open cookie settings</button>
  </p>
  <noscript>
    <p class="alert alert-info">JavaScript is disabled, so no optional cookies can be set and the settings panel is unavailable. Only strictly necessary cookies are used.</p>
  </noscript>
  <p>
    You can also delete or block cookies in your browser settings. Blocking strictly necessary cookies
    will prevent you from logging in.
  </p>
  <p>
    We keep an anonymous record of each consent decision (a random ID, your choices, the policy version
    and a timestamp - no IP address) so that we can demonstrate consent as required by GDPR Article 7.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If we change the cookies we use, we update the policy version and ask for your consent again.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions? Email <a href="mailto:<%= contactEmail %>"><%= contactEmail %></a>.</p>
</article>
